# Evidence landing and repository location

## Session start

- Resolve the repository's absolute physical path before changing files.
- Stop if that path begins with an iCloud Drive or Dropbox sync root.
- Common macOS sync roots include `/Users/<user>/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/`, `/Users/<user>/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/`, and `/Users/<user>/Dropbox/`.
- Do not create, copy, or move a repository worktree into a synced path.

## Evidence changes

- If a session creates or re-seals an artefact under `evidence/` or in a `control/` directory, commit and push all authorised evidence changes before the session ends.
- If a safe evidence commit or push cannot complete, create and commit a dated WIP note under `docs/codex-program/notes/`.
- The WIP note must name every uncommitted path and explain why each path remains uncommitted.
- Do not report the evidence as landed when the WIP-note route was used.

## Session end

- Run `git status --short`.
- End only when the result is empty or every remaining path is deliberately excluded and explained.
- Name every deliberate exclusion in the final report.
